    "status": "present",
    "value": "Return a fresh tree with the same BST shape where each value becomes the sum of original values greater than or equal to it. The approach is: clone then reverse-inorder accumulation; caller BST remains unchanged. Its target cost is O(n) time/O(n) fresh output and stack. Treat the invariant underlying that approach as the reason each local update preserves the required result. Check it against an independent bounded reference before relying on large-domain constructions."
  },
